    "summary": "I fixed two bugs in `cache/lru.py`, and the tests pass (2 passed).\n\n- **`get`:** a successful read now moves the key to the most-recently-used position. Before, reads never refreshed an entry, so recently used entries were still evicted.\n- **`put`:** updating a key that's already cached no longer evicts another entry. It just refreshes that key's position. Eviction now only happens when a new key is added to a full cache.\n\nThe public API is unchanged.",
